# time() with a zone, from the softcode audit (#2268): UTC, a whole number of hours and a fractional one
# are zones, and anything that is neither a zone nor an object is an invalid time zone.
::case time.login
::login wiz Wiz wizpass
think ok

::case time.zone  time() reads UTC and numeric offsets as zones
think [lte(abs(sub(convtime(time(utc),UTC),secs())),2)]
think [lte(abs(add(sub(convtime(time(-8),UTC),convtime(time(utc),UTC)),28800)),2)]
think [lte(abs(sub(sub(convtime(time(5.5),UTC),convtime(time(utc),UTC)),19800)),2)]
think [time(Nowhere/Atlantis)]
think [time(24)]
